The origin chat of a cross-gateway dispatch painted green with an empty task list while 13 cards ran
on another gateway. Two predicates existed: the sidebar count walked the hub replica (rel shepherd +
children), the task list read local boards only, and a review card or a failed replica read counted
as nothing. Now _remote_links is the single source for kanban_active/kanban_blocked (which also gate
archive) and for /api/session-kanban-tasks: owner-qualified rows (gateway/board/id key, via
shepherd|descendant, root, synced_at, stale). review counts as unfinished locally and remotely. A
stale replica keeps last-known rows marked stale (kanban_remote_stale); an unreadable one keeps the
last good answer, never zero.
